  "narration": "Why does this window turn into a mirror at night? Watch the glass. Sunlight shoots straight through it and hits your eyes. Inside the room, light from your face hits the same pane, bounces off, and comes right back to you. Both pictures reach your eyes at once. By day, the bright street buries your reflection. But after sunset the street goes dark. Click on your lamp and your reflection wins. That's your face looking right back at you, and that is exactly…",
